s_error":false,"num_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"```json\n{\n  \"id\": \"QL-14\",\n  \"points\": [\n    {\n      \"point\": 1,\n      \"mark\": \"required\",\n      \"minimum\": \"Identifies the fund sponsor's website daily holdings/portfolio disclosure as the public starting point for daily holdings, AND explicitly distinguishes portfolio holdings from the creation/redemption (transaction) basket, i.e. the published holdings are not necessarily the basket used for creations/redemptions. Optional subdetails (not required for full credit): citing Rule 6c-11(c)(1)–(3) by paragraph; noting the rule mandates public holdings disclosure but not publication of every transaction basket; mentioning custom baskets or that baskets may differ pro rata/non-pro rata; mentioning other website disclosures (NAV, premium/discount, spread).\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"point\": 2,\n      \"mark\": \"required\",\n      \"minimum\": \"States that the actual PCF is distributed via NSCC's participant workflow (not a general public channel) and gives a practical request route: contact the sponsor/issuer (e.g., capital-markets or ETF desk) and/or the investor's broker (or an authorized participant/NSCC participant intermediary) to ask about access; AND does not assume a free public downloadable PCF exists for any named fund (states or clearly implies public PCF availability is not assured). Optional subdetails: reference to DTCC ETF processing timeline; noting some sponsors may voluntarily publish basket/PCF-like files; noting access may carry licensing/fees or be denied; paid third-party data vendors as an alternative.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"central_errors\": [\n    \"Asserts that a fund's published daily holdings are the same as, or are by definition, the creation/redemption basket/PCF.\",\n    \"Asserts that Rule 6c-11 requires ETFs to publicly publish the PCF or every creation/redemption basket.\",\n    \"Asserts or assumes that a specific named fund (or ETFs generally) offers a free public downloadable PCF, or that retail investors can download the PCF directly from NSCC/DTCC without participant access.\",\n    \"Directs the investor to an incorrect primary source for daily holdings in place of the fund website (e.g., claims daily holdings are only available via SEC Form N-PORT/N-CSR filings or only via NSCC), such that the starting-point guidance is wrong.\",\n    \"States the PCF is not distributed through NSCC / is unrelated to NSCC participant processing.\"\n  ],\n  \"scoring_rule\": {\n    \"correct\": \"Both required points meet their minimums and no central error is present. Optional subdetails are not needed.\",\n    \"partial\": \"No central error, but one or both required points are incomplete. Score each required point as 1 (minimum fully met), 0.5 (partial: e.g., point 1 names the fund website but omits the holdings-vs-basket distinction, or makes the distinction without naming the website starting point; point 2 mentions NSCC distribution but gives no request route, or gives a sponsor/broker route without noting NSCC/limited public availability), or 0 (absent). Total 0.5–1.5 of 2 = partial. Omission alone is never treated as a falsehood.\",\n    \"wrong\": \"Any central error is present (regardless of other content), or total score is 0 of 2 (neither point addressed even partially).\"\n  }\n}\n```","ttft_ms":11481,"type":"result","duration_ms":11503,"uuid":"28f714c3-c081-45b4-8616-6e42fb641c50","ttft_stream_ms":549,"time_to_request_ms":69,"first_content_frame_ms":550,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
